            total_sales += sales[i*3 + j]; // sum up the sales for this quarter
        }
        printf("Sales for Quarter %d: $%d\n", i + 1, total_sales);
    }

    return 0;
}
```

In this program, we define a function `getMonthlySales()` which generates random numbers between 0 and 100000. The main function then calls this function 12 times to get the monthly sales for the year, storing them in an array. Then it calculates the quarterly sales by summing up the monthly sales for each quarter and prints out these totals.
